Subject: Build without ICU while retaining the adapter's locale entry points

Base: rusty_v8 v0.106.0 (e9f20a2493883b53cb58b19a2fe761358dd57996).

build.sh disables V8 internationalization with v8_enable_i18n_support=false
and icu_use_data_file=false. The upstream adapter still unconditionally
includes an ICU header and defines two ICU locale wrappers, so those GN
settings alone are insufficient to build rusty_v8 without ICU.

Guard the include and ICU implementations with V8_INTL_SUPPORT, preserving
upstream behavior when ICU is enabled. When it is disabled, retain the two
C ABI entry points with a diagnostic and abort. The stock Rust crate emits
locale wrappers in an object that also contains ordinary V8 helpers. COFF
linkers resolve that object's undefined symbols before discarding unused
functions, so removing the C definitions breaks even consumers that never
call ICU. /OPT:REF does not fix this. Optimized Rust LTO can remove the
wrappers earlier, but linking must not depend on optimization or profile.

The retained entry points do not emulate ICU: get_language_tag and
set_default_locale have no error return, so abort rather than silently
returning a fabricated locale or ignoring a request. They add no ICU code
or data. set_common_data_73 is a separate, inline Rust wrapper around an
ICU-owned symbol; that symbol remains absent and calling it cannot link.
All three Rust ICU APIs remain unsupported. V8's non-ICU date/time-zone
fallback remains; RegExp, the JS parser and other engines are unchanged.

Validation: build with the two GN settings and run ci/probe.rs through the
stock consumer without LTO. It links both locale APIs, calls each in a
child process and checks the failure diagnostic, then verifies that Intl
is absent and WasmGC executes. On upgrade, check for equivalent feature
guards and changed ICU entry points. Remove the fail-fast definitions if
the downstream Rust binding can omit the unsupported APIs at compile time.

Upstream adapter, Rust ICU API, and COFF linker resolution order:
https://github.com/denoland/rusty_v8/blob/v0.106.0/src/binding.cc
https://github.com/denoland/rusty_v8/blob/v0.106.0/src/icu.rs
https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/blob/llvmorg-21.1.5/lld/COFF/Driver.cpp#L2678

--- a/src/binding.cc
+++ b/src/binding.cc
@@ -4,12 +4,15 @@
 #include <cstddef>
 #include <cstdint>
 #include <cstdio>
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <iostream>
 #include <memory>
 
 #include "cppgc/platform.h"
 #include "support.h"
+#ifdef V8_INTL_SUPPORT
 #include "unicode/locid.h"
+#endif
 #include "v8-callbacks.h"
 #include "v8/include/cppgc/persistent.h"
 #include "v8/include/libplatform/libplatform.h"
@@ -3737,6 +3740,7 @@
 // icu
 
 extern "C" {
+#ifdef V8_INTL_SUPPORT
 
 size_t icu_get_default_locale(char* output, size_t output_len) {
   const icu_73::Locale& default_locale = icu::Locale::getDefault();
@@ -3753,6 +3757,18 @@
   icu::Locale::setDefault(icu::Locale(locale), status);
 }
 
+#else
+// COFF linking needs these definitions even if the Rust wrappers are unused.
+size_t icu_get_default_locale(char*, size_t) {
+  std::fputs("rusty_v8: icu_get_default_locale requires ICU support\n", stderr);
+  std::abort();
+}
+
+void icu_set_default_locale(const char*) {
+  std::fputs("rusty_v8: icu_set_default_locale requires ICU support\n", stderr);
+  std::abort();
+}
+#endif  // V8_INTL_SUPPORT
 }  // extern "C"
 
 // v8::PropertyDescriptor
